id: pm-atnfh4
title: "GH-1008: assurance measurements accept unknown source kinds and contracts hide the valid vocabulary"
description: "The assurance registry persists a measurement whose source.kind is outside the SDK vocabulary, allowing an apparently enforced gate that can never resolve. The public SDK schema, CLI/MCP mutation boundary, and command-scoped contract discovery must share one authoritative source-kind enumeration."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:cli","area:sdk",assurance,contracts,discoverability,regression
created_at: "2026-08-14T06:11:31.628Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:47.486Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:07.695Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-14T07:56:07.695Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: One exported SDK vocabulary defines every supported assurance measurement source kind; SDK registry writes reject an unknown source.kind before any bytes or history are written; CLI and MCP expose the same typed refusal and supported values; pm contracts --command assurance returns a useful command-scoped result under its declared default budget; Unit integration contract and packed temporary-project tests prove valid kinds persist and invalid kinds do not
parent: pm-1jzupz
risk: critical
confidence: 98
reporter: GitHub issue #1008
severity: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Unknown measurement source kinds are rejected atomically with the supported vocabulary and the command-scoped contract fits its default budget.
actual_result: source.kind bogus is persisted successfully and the documented contract lookup omits its result under the default budget.
affected_version: 2026.8.14
regression: true
customer_impact: A project can store and advertise a quality gate whose measurement can never be evaluated.
